Drop creature_template immunity to damage-dealing mechanics (bleed, disease).
Touches: src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.h, src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp

Why: player report -- "just like elemental immunities, nothing should be
immune to bleed damage either", then "or any type of damage".

Core-patch 0017 already handled damage SCHOOLS, which is why the report is
phrased as a comparison to it. Schools and mechanics are separate systems and
0017 does not touch the second one. Bleed-proof is not a school immunity:
Rend, Rupture, Garrote and Lacerate are physical spells carrying
MECHANIC_BLEED, and an undead or elemental with template mechanic immunity
refuses the aura outright in IsImmunedToSpell / IsImmunedToSpellEffect,
which runs long before anything 0017 changed.

Scope decision, and the reason this is not simply "all mechanics":

The literal reading of "any type of damage" would mean softening every
mechanic in m_spellImmune[IMMUNITY_MECHANIC]. That set is mostly crowd
control -- stun, fear, root, polymorph, banish, silence, knockback. Dropping
those would make every raid boss in the game stunnable, which deletes
encounter design across all of WotLK and is plainly not what a report about
bleed damage was asking for. So the softening covers the mechanics that
classify DAMAGE:

    MECHANIC_BLEED      Rend, Rupture, Garrote, Lacerate, Deep Wounds
    MECHANIC_INFECTED   disease damage-over-time

Control mechanics stay enforced. If a report later says a specific boss
should be stunnable, that is a different and much narrower change.

Same template-versus-aura split as 0017, using the same signal:
Creature::LoadTemplateImmunities registers template entries under the
sentinel spell id (uint32 max), so a scripted invulnerability phase (a real
aura) still works, and if a creature holds both, the aura wins.

Known limit, inherited from 0017: mechanic immunity is binary -- it refuses
the aura or it does not -- so there is no partial to downgrade to. A bleed
now lands at full damage rather than at an 80% resist. Bleeds are physical,
and CalcAbsorbResist's resist block does not run for SPELL_SCHOOL_MASK_NORMAL
anyway, so the school version could not have given it a partial either.

Gated by the existing LivingGear.SoftenCreatureImmunity (default 1) -- same
switch as 0017, because it is the same decision.

--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.h
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.h
@@ next to LivingGearSoftenedSchoolImmunity
+    [[nodiscard]] bool LivingGearSoftenedMechanicImmunity(uint32 mechanic) const;

--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp
@@ above Unit::LivingGearSoftenedSchoolImmunity
+static bool LivingGear_IsDamageMechanic(uint32 mechanic)
+{
+    switch (mechanic)
+    {
+        case MECHANIC_BLEED:
+        case MECHANIC_INFECTED:
+            return true;
+        default:
+            return false;
+    }
+}
+
+bool Unit::LivingGearSoftenedMechanicImmunity(uint32 mechanic) const
+{
+    static uint32 constexpr templateSpellId = std::numeric_limits<uint32>::max();
+
+    if (!mechanic || !IsCreature() || !LivingGear_IsDamageMechanic(mechanic))
+        return false;
+    if (!LivingGear_SoftenCreatureImmunity())
+        return false;
+
+    bool fromTemplate = false;
+    for (auto const& [immunityMechanic, immunityAuraId] : m_spellImmune[IMMUNITY_MECHANIC])
+    {
+        if (immunityMechanic != mechanic)
+            continue;
+        if (immunityAuraId == templateSpellId)
+            fromTemplate = true;
+        else
+            return false;   // a real aura says immune, and it wins
+    }
+    return fromTemplate;
+}

@@ Unit::IsImmunedToSpell, the whole-spell mechanic check
-        if (mechanicList.count(mechanic) > 0)
+        if (mechanicList.count(mechanic) > 0 && !LivingGearSoftenedMechanicImmunity(mechanic))
             return true;

@@ Unit::IsImmunedToSpellEffect, the per-effect mechanic check
-        if (mechanicList.count(mechanic) > 0)
+        if (mechanicList.count(mechanic) > 0 && !LivingGearSoftenedMechanicImmunity(mechanic))
             return true;
